From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 9 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fold the players of the Duel library from SkipPhase to
 the end for n > 2

Lua sees only 0, 1, PLAYER_NONE and PLAYER_ALL while a duelist acts.
This commit turns those values into core seats in the second half of libduel.cpp.
With 2 duelists or no scope every helper is the identity, so n == 2 does not change.

A player that chooses (Select*, Announce*, SelectOption) goes through unfold_action.
At n > 2 a chooser that is not a living duelist gets the stock empty result.
No prompt goes to an eliminated seat.
SelectDisableField, SelectFieldZone, SelectOption, AnnounceType and AnnounceCoin
write the real seat into argument 1, because their continuation reads it again.
Field readers (the Get/IsExisting Matching/Target group, field group, overlay)
use field_side and exchange the two location arguments for the value 1.
Selectors with a second player argument (SelectMatchingCard, SelectTarget) fold both.
The IsPlayerCan* family and the activity counters use query_list: best case over the opponents.
Operation info keeps 0x10, stores PLAYER_ALL once, and returns the folded player.
Release group, tribute, TossCoin, TossDice, TagSwap and the like use unfold_action.
RockPaperScissors returns PLAYER_NONE at n > 2 when seat 0 or 1 is out.
Readjust and MajesticCopy have no player and are left as they are.
The helpers are static f3b_ functions before SkipPhase.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
